LazInk licensing
================

LazInk contains code under two licenses. This is a per-file distinction,
not a choice to use either license for the entire package.

1. MPL 1.1: inkhtml.pas and its renderer implementation include inktables.inc.
   inkhtml.pas contains code derived from Project JEDI's JVCL. Its modifications
   remain under the Mozilla Public License 1.1. See LICENSES/MPL-1.1.txt,
   THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, and docs/RENDERER_CHANGES.md.

2. MIT: independently authored LazInk components and supporting code,
   examples, tests, and documentation, except for the MPL files above and
   material carrying its own upstream notice. See LICENSES/MIT.txt.

The MIT permission does not relicense third-party material. Upstream notices
and license texts retain their original terms. Lazarus/LCL and Free Pascal
are dependencies with their own licenses; they are not relicensed by LazInk.

Distribution of the MPL-covered renderer, including in compiled applications,
requires compliance with MPL 1.1. Include the applicable notices and license,
document modifications, and make the corresponding covered source available
to recipients as described in sections 3.1-3.6. The full license controls.
Independent application files need not become MPL merely because they use
LazInk; section 3.7 permits larger works under other licenses.

Source availability in this source distribution: the corresponding renderer
source is supplied in inkhtml.pas and inktables.inc alongside this file.
If distributing a binary separately, supply its corresponding covered source
and required build materials with it, or give recipients an actual source
location that satisfies MPL 1.1. A link to unmodified JVCL is not a substitute
for the source of the modified renderer used to build that binary.
